# Morgantha at home (docs/voice/morgantha.md): the loft of Old Bonegrinder, rocking between the cages. The region's
# turning point: buy the children back (gold, a dream, a promise), walk away, or fight. Whoever of her daughters is
# still at hand fights beside her (coven_last_stand). Remembers the village (morgantha.dialogue there) and the lane.

~ start
if flag.bonegrinder_bargain == "abandoned"
-> kept
endif
if flag.bonegrinder_bargain
-> after_bargain
endif
if flag.morgantha_home_met
-> again
endif
set morgantha_home_met
if not quest.children_of_the_mill
quest children_of_the_mill heard
endif
Narrator: Between the two cages, in a rocking chair worn smooth, a little old woman in a flour-dusted shawl is shelling something small and white into a bowl in her lap. She doesn't get up. The chair keeps rocking.
if flag.morgantha_driven_off
Morgantha [smile]: The brave one who chased Morgantha's cart out of the village! Morgantha told you, duckling: she remembers every face. And here's yours, come all this way to be remembered properly.
elif flag.dream_pastries_bought >= 1
Morgantha [smile]: My customers! All those stairs, just to see where the pastries come from. How are the dreams, dearies? Sweet? Of course they are.
elif flag.morgantha_met or flag.morgantha_cart_met
Morgantha [smile]: The new faces! Still lovely. A little leaner. The road does that to people.
else
Morgantha [smile]: Visitors! Up all those stairs and not one of you carrying a basket. Never mind. Morgantha has plenty.
endif
if flag.dream_pastry_eaten
Morgantha [sly]: And you had the free sample, pet. Morgantha has looked in on your dreams since. You were smiling.
endif
if species:halfling
interject species:halfling: She's looking at me like a ham again.
endif
-> family

~ again
Morgantha [smile]: Back again, dearies? Morgantha knew you would be. Everybody comes back.
-> family

~ family
if flag.offalia_slain
Morgantha [sad]: And you broke my Offalia. She was the slow one, dearies, but she was mine. Morgantha is adding that to your account.
elif flag.offalia_asleep
Morgantha [sly]: Fed my own girl my own baking. Oh, that's clever. Morgantha likes clever. Clever keeps.
elif flag.offalia_lured
Morgantha: Sent my Offalia trotting down the hill after nobody. She'll stop at every hedge from here to Vallaki. Never mind. Morgantha can see to her own visitors.
endif
if flag.bella_pact
Narrator: The dressing table in the corner stands empty. Morgantha glances at it once, and goes on smiling, and goes on shelling.
elif flag.bella_fled
Narrator: The mirror in the corner is cracked clean across. Morgantha doesn't look at it.
endif
if flag.pastry_cart_raided
Morgantha [sly]: And somebody's had their fingers in my cart. Morgantha counts her pastries, pet. She counts everything.
endif
-> menu

~ menu
* The children. Let them go. -> children
* What are you? -> what
* [if flag.bonegrinder_recipe_read] We read your receipt book. -> receipts
* [Insight DC 13] Watch her while she talks. -> read_ok | read_fail
* Then we'll take them from you. -> fight_warning
* We're leaving. -> leaving

~ children
Morgantha: Let them go? But they're paid for, dearie. Their mother had a basket a week all season and dreamed of her little lost one every night. A child for a season. That's the custom. Everybody knows the custom.
if guest:ireena
interject guest:ireena: There's no such custom. I lived in that village all my life.
Morgantha [smile]: Then you never ran short, did you, pet? Lucky girl. He'd pay more for you than for any pastry.
endif
Morgantha: But Morgantha is fair. Ask anybody. You may buy them back.
-> bargain

~ bargain
* [if gold >= 150] We'll buy them back. (150 gp) -> pay_gold
* [if not gold >= 150] We haven't that much. -> too_poor
* What else would you take? -> dream_offer
* [Persuasion DC 16] Free them, and we'll leave you and your mill in peace. -> truce_ok | truce_fail
* Keep them. We want no part of this. -> abandon
* No deals. -> menu

~ too_poor
Morgantha: Then you can't afford them, can you? Morgantha doesn't give credit. Credit is how folk end up owing children.
-> bargain

~ pay_gold
gold -150
set bonegrinder_bargain = "gold"
quest children_of_the_mill bargain_struck
Morgantha [smile]: A hundred and fifty. Their mother let them go for less, if you don't count the honey. Pleasure doing business, dearies.
-> release

~ dream_offer
Morgantha: Gold is dull, pet. Here's a better price. One dream: your sweetest, the one you save for bad nights. Morgantha draws it out like a splinter, and after that she visits now and then while you sleep. Only to sit.
* Take mine. -> dream_paid
* No. -> bargain

~ dream_paid
set bonegrinder_bargain = "dream"
quest children_of_the_mill bargain_struck
Narrator: She leans close enough that {name} can smell the honey on her, and lays one cold finger on {name}'s brow. Something small and warm goes out of {name}, and afterwards {name} can't remember what it was.
Morgantha [smile]: Delicious. Morgantha will be seeing you, duckling. Now and again. Don't wake.
-> release

~ truce_ok
set bonegrinder_bargain = "truce"
quest children_of_the_mill bargain_struck
Morgantha [sly]: Peace, from heroes. That's worth something: you're the sort who keeps a promise and hates yourselves for it. Very well. The children, for your word. Morgantha will hold you to it.
-> release

~ truce_fail
Morgantha [smile]: Peace? From you? Morgantha has peace. She has a mill, and a hill, and a valley full of hungry people. What she hasn't got is a reason.
-> bargain

~ abandon
set bonegrinder_bargain = "abandoned"
set bonegrinder_fate = "abandoned"
set pastry_trade = "thriving"
quest children_of_the_mill children_abandoned
Morgantha [smile]: Sensible. You'll go far, dearies. Not very far; it's a small valley. But far.
Narrator: Behind the bars, the girl puts an arm round her brother and watches you go. She doesn't call out. She has stopped expecting anyone to.
-> END

~ release
Narrator: Morgantha unhooks a ring of iron keys from her apron and opens both cages, humming. The children don't move until she has sat back down.
Morgantha [smile]: Off you go, ducklings. Mind the stairs. Give your mother Morgantha's love; she'll be wanting another basket soon.
-> old_bonegrinder/children:freed

~ what
Morgantha: Just an old baker, dearie, and her two girls, doing an honest trade in a hard country. Folk want sweet dreams. Morgantha sells them. Is it Morgantha's fault the dreams are better than waking?
if class:cleric
interject class:cleric: You're a night hag. You ride sleepers' dreams and steal what's left of them.
Morgantha [sly]: Such words, from such a pretty mouth. Morgantha will sit a little further off from your sun-trinket, pet, if it's all the same.
endif
if treasure_at:old_bonegrinder
Morgantha: And keep your fingers out of Morgantha's oven. There's something at the back of it that won't burn, and Morgantha doesn't care for things that won't burn.
endif
-> menu

~ receipts
Morgantha [sly]: Read the family receipts, did you? Then you know about the special flour. Every family has a secret ingredient, duckling. Ours is just more honest about it.
-> menu

~ read_ok
Narrator: She never looks at the cages. She looks at the stair, and at the corner, and at the stair again, counting her family. She is far less sure of this than she sounds, and she doesn't want to do it alone.
-> menu

~ read_fail
Narrator: She smiles. She rocks. She shells. Whatever is under that smile has had a very long time to practise staying there.
-> menu

~ leaving
Morgantha [smile]: So soon? Take a pastry for the road. No? Ah, well. Everybody comes back to Morgantha in the end.
-> END

# --- The fight: who stands with her ---

~ fight_warning
set offalia_in_last_stand = false
set bella_in_last_stand = false
if not flag.offalia_slain and not flag.offalia_asleep and not flag.offalia_lured
set offalia_in_last_stand
endif
if not flag.bella_pact and not flag.bella_fled and not flag.bella_slain
set bella_in_last_stand
endif
if flag.offalia_in_last_stand and flag.bella_in_last_stand
-> whole_coven
endif
if flag.offalia_in_last_stand or flag.bella_in_last_stand
Morgantha [smile]: Taking a poor old woman's grandchildren, in her own home. Shame on you. Girls! Mother needs you!
-> fight
endif
Morgantha [sad]: All on her own, then. Bella's sulking somewhere and Offalia's gone somewhere, and it's only Morgantha and you. Well. Morgantha has managed alone before.
-> fight

~ whole_coven
Morgantha [smile]: All three of us, dearies? Together? Oh, you are brave. Bella, pet, put down the mirror. Offalia! Visitors!
Narrator: Downstairs, something heavy stops chewing. In the corner, a stool scrapes back. Three voices begin humming the same tune, and the loft is suddenly much smaller.
* We stand by it. -> fight
* Wait. Not like this. -> menu

~ fight
if flag.offalia_in_last_stand
set offalia_slain
endif
if flag.bella_in_last_stand
set bella_slain
endif
if flag.offalia_slain and flag.bella_slain
set bonegrinder_fate = "destroyed"
set pastry_trade = "ended"
elif flag.bella_pact and not flag.bella_slain and not flag.bella_fled
set bonegrinder_fate = "bella"
set pastry_trade = "dwindling"
else
set bonegrinder_fate = "broken"
set pastry_trade = "dwindling"
endif
Morgantha [angry]: Then Morgantha will have you for the oven, and your bones for the stone, and your dreams for supper. Waste not, dearies.
combat coven_last_stand

# --- Later visits ---

~ after_bargain
Morgantha [smile]: My heroes! No more children today, dearies. There's always pastries.
if flag.bonegrinder_bargain == "truce"
Morgantha [sly]: And you gave Morgantha your word. Morgantha remembers.
endif
* Your bargaining days are over. -> broken_word
* Goodbye. -> END

~ broken_word
if flag.bonegrinder_bargain == "truce"
Narrator: A promise is a heavy thing to set down. You feel the weight of this one as you do it.
endif
-> fight_warning

~ kept
Morgantha [smile]: Back for a pastry, my sensible dearies? The little ones are keeping nicely.
* We've changed our minds about the children. -> bargain
* Then we'll take them from you. -> fight_warning
* Goodbye. -> END
